# Integer32 minimum and maximum values

Verifies the int32 boundary values through the complete CLI pipeline. The
maximum is expressible as a literal; the minimum is derived by subtracting
one from the largest negative literal because a negated minimum-magnitude
literal is validated unsigned first, consistent with int8 and int64.

>>> source
ceiling: int32 = 2147483647
floor: int32 = -2147483647
unit: int32 = 1

// Verifies the largest int32 literal prints unchanged.
print(ceiling)

// Verifies the int32 minimum is reachable through checked arithmetic.
minimum: int32 = floor - unit
print(minimum)

<<< stdout
2147483647
-2147483648

<<< stderr
